  "function_translated_nl": "Lesson context: lesson_08. Let quadrilateral ABCD be a 4-sided figure with AB = 4, CD = 4, DA = 6, where \u2220A = 90\u00b0, \u2220B = 90\u00b0, \u2220C = 90\u00b0, \u2220D = 90\u00b0. Let quadrilateral PQRS be a 4-sided figure with PQ = 6, QR = 9, RS = 6, SP = 9, where \u2220P = 90\u00b0, \u2220Q = 90\u00b0, \u2220R = 90\u00b0, \u2220S = 90\u00b0. Triangle ABCD is similar to triangle PQRS by SAS similarity with scale factor 1.5 (congruent angle pairs: A \u2245 P, B \u2245 Q, C \u2245 R, D \u2245 S). Find the length of BC in ABCD.",
  "student_facing_prose": "A contractor is designing two rectangular floor plans for similar buildings. The first building, ABCD, has dimensions AB = 4 meters, CD = 4 meters, and DA = 6 meters, with all four corners being right angles. The second building, PQRS, has dimensions PQ = 6 meters, QR = 9 meters, RS = 6 meters, and SP = 9 meters, also with all four corners being right angles.\n\nThe contractor confirms that quadrilateral ABCD is similar to quadrilateral PQRS by the SAS similarity criterion, with a scale factor of 1.5. The corresponding angles are congruent: \u2220A \u2245 \u2220P, \u2220B \u2245 \u2220Q, \u2220C \u2245 \u2220R, and \u2220D \u2245 \u2220S.\n\nTo complete the floor plan for building ABCD, what is the length of side BC?"
